            <div xml:id="d393">

                <pb facs="0486" n="388" xml:id="pg388"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Commission/604: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Acting Chairman of the American Delegation to the General Disarmament
                        Conference (Gibson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-12-05T12:00:00-05:00">December 5,
                        1932—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. For Davis and Wilson. Your 56, December 4, 10
                    p.m., and Department’s 44, December 4, midnight. I concur in your estimate and
                    in your conclusions set forth in penultimate paragraph.</p>
                <p>I approve of your talking strictly confidentially in your discretion with chief
                    delegates of Great Britain and France as suggested in concluding paragraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
